# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Read top to bottom; first match wins.
#
# Pages already serves /audit for audit.html without any rule here, and the
# Node server does the same by rewriting extensionless paths. These exist so
# the .html form does not become a second, competing URL for the same page.

/index.html      /            301
/quickstart.html /quickstart  301
/sdk.html        /sdk         301
/policy.html     /policy      301
/audit.html      /audit       301

# The app lives on its own host. These ten pages are static files on a CDN;
# the dashboard, the approval pages and the OAuth callback are a function on
# Vercel, and adeia.xyz forwards to it rather than duplicating it.
#
# 302 rather than 301 on purpose. This is deployment topology, not a canonical
# URL, and a browser that has cached a permanent redirect to a host we later
# move off is a browser that cannot be told otherwise.
#
# Apply these only once the Vercel deployment answers — until then they point
# at a host that does not exist. See docs/deploy.md.
/dashboard      https://app.adeia.xyz/dashboard          302
/dashboard/*    https://app.adeia.xyz/dashboard/:splat   302
/approvals/*    https://app.adeia.xyz/approvals/:splat   302
/auth/*         https://app.adeia.xyz/auth/:splat        302
